---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "About" }];
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="About HomeDIYCalc: free home improvement calculators that run entirely in your browser. No signup, no cost; calculations stay in your browser."
  canonical="/about/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">About HomeDIYCalc</h1>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-slate-700">
    <p>
      HomeDIYCalc is a free set of calculators for home improvement projects. It answers
      the question every DIYer asks at the start of a job: <em>how much material do I
      actually need?</em> — concrete for a slab, paint for a room, gravel for a driveway,
      tile for a floor — and turns the answer into a shopping list you can take to the store.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Who runs HomeDIYCalc</h2>
    <p>
      HomeDIYCalc is operated independently by an individual based in
      Malaysia. It is not a company — just one person building a free tool
      for homeowners and DIY users, primarily in the United States. The
      calculators are free, there are no accounts, and nothing is sold. If
      you need to reach the operator, see the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">What makes it different</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Free, no signup.</strong> Every calculator works without an account, a login, or a payment.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Transparent math.</strong> Each calculator page shows its formula, so you can check the result yourself.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Rounds up, never down.</strong> Package quantities — bags, boxes, gallons — are always rounded up from the calculated amount, so the calculator itself never recommends a fraction of a package. The result is still an estimate for the measurements you enter — confirm quantities with your supplier before ordering.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Imperial and metric.</strong> Enter measurements in feet and gallons or in meters and liters; switch at any time without losing your numbers.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-slate-900">No invented prices.</strong> Cost estimates appear only when you enter your own local prices. If you enter no price, no cost is shown.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">How the site works</h2>
    <p>
      The site is a fully static website: pages are generated at build time and every
      calculation runs in your browser in plain TypeScript. There is no backend, no
      database, and no external service involved in a calculation. Saved items in My Project
      live only in your own browser (LocalStorage).
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">What the calculators do not do</h2>
    <p>
      Calculators are estimates, not professional advice. They do not account for every
      site condition — slope, compaction, spillage, damaged material, or local building
      codes. Always confirm quantities with your supplier and, for structural work, with a
      qualified professional. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Status</h2>
    <p>
      The site foundation is built (Phase 1), and all 31 calculators are live — 10 in
      Phase 2, 8 in Phase 3, 7 in Phase 4, 1 (Stair Calculator) in Phase 15, and 5 landscaping calculators in Phase 17. See <a href="/calculators/">All Calculators</a> for
      the full list.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
